          "from": "Old Norse gata 'street' (Old Danish gatæ)",
          "to": "gade /ɡaːðə/"
        },
        {
          "from": "Old Norse bíta 'to bite' (Old Danish bitæ)",
          "to": "bide /biːðə/"
        },
        {
          "from": "Old Norse hvítr 'white'",
          "to": "hvid /ˈviːˀð/"
        },
        {
          "from": "Old Norse matr 'food'",
          "to": "mad /mað/"
        },
        {
          "from": "Old Norse fótr 'foot'",
          "to": "fod [ˈfoˀð]",
          "note": "Danish lenition weakened postvocalic t to the 'soft d' /ð/, still spelled d; Swedish and Norwegian keep t (gata, bita, vit, mat, fot)."
